    "question": "Rayden bought three times as many ducks as Lily from the market. He also bought four times as many geese as Lily. If Lily bought 20 ducks and 10 geese, how many more ducks and geese do Rayden have more than Lily altogether?",
    "gold": "70",
    "answer": "If Rayden bought three times as many ducks as Lily, then he has 3*20 = <<3*20=60>>60 ducks\nHe has 60-20 = <<60-20=40>>40 more ducks than Lily has.\nRayden also bought 4*10 = <<4*10=40>>40 geese, four times the geese that Lily bought.\nHe has 40-10= <<40-10=30>>30 more ducks than Lily.\nAltogether, Rayden has 30+40 = <<30+40=70>>70 more ducks and geese than Lily.\n#### 70"
  },
  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine how many more ducks and geese Rayden has compared to Lily, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the number of ducks Rayden bought.\n2. Calculate the number of geese Rayden bought.\n3. Determine the total number of ducks and geese Lily has.\n4. Determine the total number of ducks and geese Rayden has.\n5. Find the difference between the total number of ducks and geese Rayden has and the total number of ducks and geese Lily has.\n\nFirst, we calculate the number of ducks Rayden bought. Since Rayden bought three times as many ducks as Lily, and Lily bought 20 ducks, we have:\n\\[ \\text{Number of ducks Rayden bought} = 3 \\times 20 = 60 \\]\n\nNext, we calculate the number of geese Rayden bought. Since Rayden bought four times as many geese as Lily, and Lily bought 10 geese, we have:\n\\[ \\text{Number of geese Rayden bought} = 4 \\times 10 = 40 \\]\n\nNow, we determine the total number of ducks and geese Lily has:\n\\[ \\text{Total number of ducks and geese Lily has} = 20 + 10 = 30 \\]\n\nNext, we determine the total number of ducks and geese Rayden has:\n\\[ \\text{Total number of ducks and geese Rayden has} = 60 + 40 = 100 \\]\n\nFinally, we find the difference between the total number of ducks and geese Rayden has and the total number of ducks and geese Lily has:\n\\[ \\text{Difference} = 100 - 30 = 70 \\]\n\nThus, Rayden has \\(\\boxed{70}\\) more ducks and geese than Lily altogether.",
